KG42.register("rules-4055b691d367f062101e6fdd",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R003","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R003","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"Requested quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a nonnegative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. Offered quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a negative net-energy bid at the relevant time step. The coordinator must provide and operate the trading platform and its associated metering mechanisms. Scope: Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. The coordinator does not control devices directly and applies unified rules fairly to all participants. Scope: Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. Condition: When the heuristic techniques interfere with participants' control of their devices. Handling physical-network problems such as overvoltage and congestion is outside the coordinator's modeled remit and is deferred to further research. Scope: Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework. | Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. | Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework. | SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g06-e12","v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Requested quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a nonnegative net-energy bid at the relevant time step.","expression":"e^{bid} = \\left\\{ e_t^{bid} \\mid e_t^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^{*} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis} \\right) + P_t^{must\\text{-}run} - P_{PV,t},\\; t \\in T \\right\\} \\quad (A18); \\quad \\mathcal{PA}^{+}_{t} = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \\ge 0,\\; n \\in \\mathcal{PA} \\} \\quad (A23)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Offered quantities represented in the SDR energy-bid profile are submitted to the local coordinator at every iteration. Scope: SDR iterative submission of signed net-energy profiles within an energy sharing region. Condition: The submitted profile contains a negative net-energy bid at the relevant time step.","expression":"e^{bid} = \\left\\{ e_t^{bid} \\mid e_t^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^{*} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis} \\right) + P_t^{must\\text{-}run} - P_{PV,t},\\; t \\in T \\right\\} \\quad (A18); \\quad \\mathcal{PA}^{-}_{t} = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0,\\; n \\in \\mathcal{PA} \\} \\quad (A22)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-04","v141-b-g07-ev-05"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator must provide and operate the trading platform and its associated metering mechanisms. Scope: Coordinator infrastructure obligations in the described local P2P framework.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The coordinator does not control devices directly and applies unified rules fairly to all participants. Scope: Coordinator intervention under the paper's heuristic convergence techniques. Condition: When the heuristic techniques interfere with participants' control of their devices.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E14"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Handling physical-network problems such as overvoltage and congestion is outside the coordinator's modeled remit and is deferred to further research. Scope: Limits of the coordinator's modeled remit in the studied P2P framework.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g06-e12"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":"996","section":"3.1","anchor_text":"gy sharing paradigm d P2P energy sharing paradigms. P2P energy sharing can be carried out among pros","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"P2P energy sharing can be carried out among prosumers in a microgrid or a part of distribution network (referred to as \"energy sharing region (ESR)\" in this paper), supervised by a market operator (named \"energy sharing coordinator\", short as \"coordinator\", in this paper). A coordinator is usually needed in P2P energy sharing practice due to two reasons. First of all, a coordinator is needed to specify the rules for trading and supervise the energy sharing activities. The rules include the core pricing model and implementation process, as well as other relevant rules to guarantee the interests of every participant. Secondly, a trading platform as well as the associated metering and billing mechanisms needs to be provided and operated by a coordinator, based on which P2P energy sharing is able to be conducted."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p09-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":9,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3.3.1","anchor_text":"he tinguishing features are able to be kept. Secondly, although the step by length control technique","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-09.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Last but not least, even if the full control is interfered, it is interfered indirectly and fairly, i.e. the coordinator does not control any device directly but just issues unified rules (e.g. bid change limitation in the step length control technique) fairly to everyone."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g06-e12","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p23-c2r4__v141-a-M04-pricing","page":23,"printed_page":null,"section":"6","anchor_text":"he forecast for the future. In fact, there may be signiﬁcant un- ee certainties in renewable generat","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-23.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"(3) The energy sharing coordinator was considered as a market operator that only took care of energy trading. Further research is to analyse and tackle the physical problems (e.g. over voltage and congestion) in the power networks along with P2P energy sharing."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-04","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r2__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.1","anchor_text":"p g y ⎫ ∈ T ⎬⎭ (A18) he decision-making model consisting of Formulas (A1)–(A17). With the energy ell","equation_id":"A18","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the SDR mechanism, prosumers are required to provide energy bids for the coordinator at every iteration. Specifically, based on the results of the decision-making model presented in Section A.1, the energy bid of a prosumer is given by\n\ne^{bid} = \\left\\{ e_t^{bid} \\mid e_t^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis} \\right) + P_t^{must-run} - P_{PV,t}, t \\in T \\right\\}  (A18)\n\nin which x^* = \\{x_{\\delta,t}^*, x_t^{ch*}, x_t^{dis*}\\}, \\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f, t \\in T are the optimal solution of the decision-making model consisting of Formulas (A1)-(A17)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-05","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.1","anchor_text":"(A22) (A23) il price between the coordinator and the retailer as illustrated in Fig. 2; SDR haring r","equation_id":"A19-A23","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the energy bids from all the prosumers, the coordinator calculates the internal selling price by\n\np_t^{sell} = \\begin{cases} \\frac{r_t^{export} \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{(r_t^{retail} - r_t^{export}) \\cdot SDR_t + r_t^{export}}, & 0 \\le SDR_t \\le 1 \\\\ r_t^{export}, & SDR_t > 1 \\end{cases}  (A19)\n\nand the internal buying price by\n\np_t^{buy} = \\begin{cases} p_t^{sell} \\cdot SDR_t + r_t^{retail}(1 - SDR_t), & 0 \\le SDR_t \\le 1 \\\\ r_t^{export}, & SDR_t > 1 \\end{cases}  (A20)\n\nin which\n\nSDR_t = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^-} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}}  (A21)\n\nwhere\n\n\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^- = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}  (A22)\n\nand\n\n\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+ = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \\ge 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}.  (A23)\n\nIn Formulas (A19)-(A23), r_t^{export} and r_t^{retail} are the export and retail price between the coordinator and the retailer as illustrated in Fig. 2; SDR represents the supply and demand ratio of the whole P2P energy sharing region. Formulas (A19)-(A23) establish the pricing model in the coordinator agent under the SDR mechanism."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"Rule v141-c-R003 is a coordination-stage rule whose constraints describe (i) the coordinator's receipt of SDR energy bids and (ii) its non-optimising role obligations. None of C001-C005 defines a design or operational decision variable owned by this rule: the coordinator does not control devices and solves no optimisation here, and the submitted net-energy bid e^{bid}_{n,t} appearing in C001/C002 is the output of the prosumer decision model (Formulas A1-A18), whose decision variables (x_{delta,t}, x_t^{ch}, x_t^{dis}) are owned by the bidding/clearing rules rather than by this coordination rule. Declaring them here would be cross-rule reuse of a shared symbol. The frozen C.1 draft likewise recorded no typed variable node for this rule (field_notes: 'Typed variable objects are outside this graph draft; this does not assert that the source lacks variables').","empty_theta_reason":"This rule's constraints introduce no fixed constant or input parameter of their own. The only numeric object in the formalized conditions is the implicit sign threshold 0 appearing in the source set definitions (Formulas A22/A23), which is a literal constant rather than a named parameter. The other quantities occurring inside the transcribed bid definition (eta^{ch}, eta^{dis}, P^{must-run}, P^{PV}) are prosumer decision-model inputs defined in Appendix A.1 and owned by the bidding/clearing rules, so they are not re-declared as this rule's parameters. The frozen C.1 draft also recorded no typed parameter node for this rule (field_notes: 'Typed parameter objects are outside this graph draft; this does not assert that the source lacks parameters')."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M02-pricing","v141-a-M03-bidding"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-04","quote":"In the SDR mechanism, prosumers are required to provide energy bids for the coordinator at every iteration."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-04","quote":"e_t^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis} \\right) + P_t^{must-run} - P_{PV,t}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-05","quote":"\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^+ = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \\ge 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-04","quote":"In the SDR mechanism, prosumers are required to provide energy bids for the coordinator at every iteration."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-04","quote":"e_t^{bid} = \\left( \\sum_{\\delta \\in \\mathcal{A}_f} x_{\\delta,t}^* \\right) + \\left( \\frac{x_t^{ch*}}{\\eta^{ch}} + x_t^{dis*} \\eta^{dis} \\right) + P_t^{must-run} - P_{PV,t}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-05","quote":"\\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}^- = \\{ n \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A} \\}"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","quote":"Secondly, a trading platform as well as the associated metering and billing mechanisms needs to be provided and operated by a coordinator, based on which P2P energy sharing is able to be conducted."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E14","quote":"even if the full control is interfered, it is interfered indirectly and fairly, i.e. the coordinator does not control any device directly but just issues unified rules (e.g. bid change limitation in the step length control technique) fairly to everyone."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g06-e12","quote":"The energy sharing coordinator was considered as a market operator that only took care of energy trading. Further research is to analyse and tackle the physical problems (e.g. over voltage and congestion) in the power networks along with P2P energy sharing."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"73a15ce17bb7293c3b9ac41e6c0890c866b15b5aca479c00123843ea003ae2c1","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Coordination-stage rule v141-c-R003 ('Local market coordinator', mechanism v141-a-M01) formalizes the local energy-sharing coordinator's receipt of SDR energy bids and its role obligations. The demand-side (C001) and supply-side (C002) submission constraints have direct source support in the supplied evidence: Formula (A18) defines the net-energy bid e^{bid} that prosumers supply to the coordinator at every iteration, and Formulas (A23)/(A22) partition the submitted bids by sign into the demand set PA^+ (e^{bid}_{n,t} >= 0) and the supply set PA^- (e^{bid}_{n,t} \u003c 0). These are transcribed faithfully (formalization_origin=source) with signs, indices and quantifiers preserved. Constraints C003 (platform/metering/billing provision), C004 (non-intrusive, fair unified rules) and C005 (physical-network problems out of modelled remit) are procedural/scope statements with no mathematical expression in the supplied evidence and remain not_formalized with expression=null. The rule introduces no optimisation/decision variable of its own and no fixed parameter of its own, so x and theta are empty. B evidence is UNREVIEWED in this experiment (source_status=unverified, audit_performed=false); the transcription relies only on the supplied quotations and no independent source review of B or of this scientific output has been performed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E001"],"rationale":"C001 formalizes the demand-side net-energy bid (requested quantities, e^{bid}_{n,t} >= 0 by source Formulas A18 and A23) submitted by prosumers to the local coordinator at every iteration. It binds node bidding.demand (the requested/demand quantity) to node coordination.local_operator (the bid-receiving coordinator), which is exactly the frozen link edge v141-c-R003-E001 (bidding.demand -> coordination.local_operator, links). No node or edge is added or reinterpreted."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","node_ids":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R003-E002"],"rationale":"C002 formalizes the supply-side net-energy bid (offered quantities, e^{bid}_{n,t} \u003c 0 by source Formulas A18 and A22) submitted by prosumers to the local coordinator at every iteration. It binds node bidding.supply (the offered/supply quantity) to node coordination.local_operator (the bid-receiving coordinator), which is exactly the frozen link edge v141-c-R003-E002 (bidding.supply -> coordination.local_operator, links). No node or edge is added or reinterpreted."}],"revision_requests":["No C.1 graph revision is requested for v141-c-R003: the bid-submission relations of C001/C002 are representable through the existing nodes (bidding.demand, bidding.supply, coordination.local_operator) and the existing link edges E001/E002; C003-C005 are procedural/scope statements that require no nodes or edges.","Unresolved/uncertain (informational): B evidence is UNREVIEWED in this experiment (audit_performed=false, source_status=unverified). Independent source verification of the transcribed Formulas (A18), (A22) and (A23) has not been performed; this formalization must not be treated as source-correct until such review occurs."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
